Input: {"question": "What type of transportation does the Karawanks Tunnel primarily serve?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d00", "start": 0, "end": 252, "text": "Karawanks Tunnel (motorway) The Karawanks Tunnel (, or \"Karavanški predor\") is a motorway tunnel crossing the Alpine Karawanks mountain range between Austria and Slovenia, with a total length of (4.89 miles), (4.98 miles) enclosure between the portals."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d00", "start": 253, "end": 314, "text": "Its construction began in 1986 and it opened on June 1, 1991."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d00", "start": 315, "end": 526, "text": "It connects the Austrian Karawanken Autobahn (A11) from Villach with the A2 motorway leading to Kranj and Ljubljana in Slovenia, decongesting the historic Loibl/Ljubelj and Wurzen/Korensko sedlo mountain passes."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d00", "start": 527, "end": 645, "text": "In the late 1970s it was planned by the Austrian Ministry of Traffic as a two-tube tunnel, (one two-lane tube for each"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d01", "start": 0, "end": 171, "text": "The Karawanks Tunnel primarily serves railway transportation and is a crucial link in the Karawanks chain of the Southern Limestone Alps, connecting Austria with Slovenia."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d01", "start": 172, "end": 341, "text": "The Loibl Pass (Loiblpass) or Ljubelj Pass (prelaz Ljubelj) is a high mountain pass in the Karawanks chain of the Southern Limestone Alps, linking Austria with Slovenia."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d01", "start": 342, "end": 422, "text": "Karawanks Tunnel (railway) and Loibl Pass are Austria–Slovenia border crossings."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d01", "start": 423, "end": 513, "text": "See Karawanks Tunnel (railway) and Loibl Pass Railway Company in the Republic of Slovenia."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d01", "start": 514, "end": 707, "text": "The Railway Company in the Republic of Slovenia (Družba za železnice v Republiki Sloveniji, DŽRS) is a joint-stock company in Slovenia that operates and maintains the Slovenian railway network."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d02", "start": 0, "end": 702, "text": "wikiPageRedirects of dbr : Karawanken_Motorway_Tunnel dbr : Karawanken_Tunnel_ ( railway ) dbr : Karawankenautobahn dbr : A11_motorway_ ( Austria ) is dbo : wikiPageWikiLink of dbr : Principal_passes_of_the_Alps dbr : List_of_longest_railway_tunnels dbr : Cerkno_Ski_Resort dbr : A2_motorway_ ( Slovenia ) dbr : Karawanken_Autobahn dbr : International_E-road_network dbr : Ten-Day_War dbr : ASFINAG dbr : Jesenice dbr : Highways_in_Slovenia dbr : Autobahns_of_Austria dbr : Podbrezje dbr : Podkoren dbr : Klek_ ( Karawanks ) dbr : Wurzen_Pass dbr : Karawanks_Tunnel dbr : Karawanken_Motorway_Tunnel dbr : Karawanken_Tunnel_ ( railway ) dbr : Karawankenautobahn dbr : A11_motorway_ ( Austria ) is foaf :"}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d02", "start": 704, "end": 713, "text": "The Karaw"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d03", "start": 0, "end": 159, "text": "Karawanks Tunnel (railway) The Karawanks Tunnel (, ) is the fourth longest railway tunnel in Austria and the longest in Slovenia with a length of (4.96 miles)."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d03", "start": 160, "end": 269, "text": "The tunnel passes under Rožca Saddle between Rosenbach in southern Austria and Jesenice in northern Slovenia."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d03", "start": 270, "end": 480, "text": "It was an important part of the Karawanken Railway, which was - together with the Bohinj Railway - built to connect the port of Trieste with Klagenfurt, the capital of the federal state of Carinthia in Austria."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d03", "start": 481, "end": 548, "text": "Between 1867-1918, Trieste was part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d03", "start": 549, "end": 612, "text": "It was Austria's first seaport and the principal outlet for the"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d04", "start": 0, "end": 506, "text": "CS1 German-language sources ( de ) All articles with dead external links Articles with dead external links from March 2025 Articles with permanently dead external links Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata Coordinates on Wikidata Articles containing German-language text Articles containing Slovene-language text All articles with unsourced statements Articles with unsourced statements from March 2010 This page was last edited on 25 March 2025 , at 03:53 ( UTC ) ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d04", "start": 507, "end": 617, "text": "Text is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License ; additional terms may apply ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d04", "start": 618, "end": 655, "text": "By using this site , you agree to the"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d05", "start": 0, "end": 69, "text": "Slovenia with a length of 7,976 metres ( 26,168 ft ) ( 4.96 miles ) ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0242-cf737d061fc5:d05", "start": 70, "end": 172, "text": "It passes under Rožca Saddle between Rosenbach in southern Austria and Jesenice in northern Slovenia ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 